            "readme_said": "npx google-surf-mcp (register in client config)",
            "actually_needed": "Use the installed binary directly (google-surf-mcp) for the MCP probe instead of npx, so no network fetch is needed at check time; handshake and health/project_memory tools work without Chrome or API key, only live browser search needs Chrome.",
            "kind": "note"
          },
          {
            "readme_said": "CLI responds to --help",
            "actually_needed": "google-surf-mcp --help does not print help; it starts the stdio MCP server and waits on stdin (the combined install && --help command hung until the 300s timeout). Use the MCP probe or the hooks subcommand instead.",
            "kind": "note"
          },
          {
            "readme_said": "Browser mode requires Google Chrome or Chromium",
            "actually_needed": "First launch logs '[google-surf-mcp] startup warm failed (will retry on first call): Chrome not found' but the server still starts, completes the MCP handshake, and answers health.",
